  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have RNA-only (config_001, acc=0.485) and multimodal (config_016, acc=0.527) baselines, showing a +4.2% gain from adding the image modality. However, we lack the image-only baseline, so we cannot decompose whether the multimodal gain comes from strong image features or from true cross-modal synergy. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly measures the standalone image contribution under the same encoder and profile settings as the multimodal runs. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 3 experiments completed, the most critical uncertainty is the relative contribution of each modality. This single experiment, combined with the existing RNA-only and multimodal results, gives a complete three-way decomposition (RNA, image, combined) that will guide all subsequent decisions—whether to invest in better image encoders (ViT), better RNA encoders (scvi/scGPT), or more sophisticated fusion. Without this baseline, exploring multiprofile or alternative encoders would be done in the dark regarding which modality is the bottleneck."
}

